DTSTAMP:20260905T151548Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260817
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260818
SUMMARY:Deadline: Copyright Agency Cultural Fund: Author Fellowship 2026
DESCRIPTION:The Copyright Agency Cultural Fund's Author Fellowship awards A
 UD 80\,000 to one established Australian author to create a significant ne
 w work for publication. ELIGIBILITY: established Australian authors with c
 ritical acclaim and confirmed publisher interest in the proposed work\; Au
 stralian residents only. This is a separate fellowship from the Cultural F
 und's Fellowship for Non-Fiction Writing\, though administered on the same
  cycle. APPLICATIONS close 17 August 2026\, 1:00pm AEST. Apply via the Cul
 tural Fund fellowship page.\n\nOrganisation: Copyright Agency (Cultural Fu
 nd)\nLocation: Australia\; Australian authors only.\nAward: AUD 80\,000 (o
 ne fellowship). No application fee.\nDuration: Fellowship to create a new 
 work\n\nMore: https://www.copyright.com.au/culturalfund/fellowship/?utm_so
 urce=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.copyright.com.au/culturalfund/fellowship/?utm_source=artifi
 cialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Australia\; Australian authors only.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:center-for-fiction-emerging-writer-fellowship-2027@artificialnouveau.gi
 thub.io
DTSTAMP:20260905T151548Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260731
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260801
SUMMARY:Deadline: The Center for Fiction / Susan Kamil Emerging Writer Fell
 owship
DESCRIPTION:The Center for Fiction / Susan Kamil Emerging Writer Fellowship
  annually supports nine early-career\, New York City-based fiction writers
  at a pivotal point in their careers. Each fellow receives a 5\,000 USD gr
 ant\, dedicated space and time to write in the Writers Studio\, personaliz
 ed editorial mentorship\, opportunities to meet literary agents\, and comm
 unity programming. Applicants must be current residents of one of the five
  boroughs and must remain in New York City for the entire fellowship year.
  An emerging writer is defined as someone who has not yet had a novel or s
 hort story collection published by a major or independent publisher and wh
 o is not currently under contract for a work of fiction\; students enrolle
 d in a degree-granting program during the fellowship year are not eligible
 . The 2027 fellowship application window opens July 1\, 2026 and closes Ju
 ly 31\, 2026.\n\nOrganisation: The Center for Fiction\nLocation: New York 
 City\, USA\nAward: USD 5\,000 grant plus writers studio space\, mentorship
 \, agent introductions\, and community programming\nDuration: One year (th
 e fellowship year)\n\nMore: https://centerforfiction.org/grants-awards/nyc
 -emerging-writers-fellowship/apply-to-the-nyc-emerging-writer-fellowship/?
 utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://centerforfiction.org/grants-awards/nyc-emerging-writers-fellows
 hip/apply-to-the-nyc-emerging-writer-fellowship/?utm_source=artificialnouv
 eaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:New York City\, USA
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:page-not-found-neu-commission-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260905T151548Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260731
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260801
SUMMARY:Deadline: NEU Commission 2026
DESCRIPTION:Page Not Found announces the third edition of the NEU Commissio
 n\, which intends to support the emergence of alternative voices within co
 ntemporary art. It targets a group currently under-represented in Europe: 
 art students with limited financial means who are required to provide a gu
 arantee for their visa and to pay high non-EU tuition fees\, economical ba
 rriers to their participation in art and knowledge production in The Nethe
 rlands. Page Not Found will commission three art students from non-Europea
 n countries to each write an essay or a free-form text in English. Each se
 lected writer receives EUR 2\,000 for the commission\, provided as an adva
 nce payment in September 2026\; the commissioned texts are published at a 
 later date. OPEN CALL: only students enrolled in Dutch art academies who a
 re NOT nationals of the European Economic Area are eligible. The commissio
 ned text does not need to be submitted when answering the open call\; the 
 jury selects recipients based on their previous writing and financial need
 . Review the Rules of the Open Call and the FAQ before applying. Deadline:
  Friday 31 July 2026\, 23:59 CEST (Amsterdam).\n\nOrganisation: Page Not F
 ound\nLocation: The Netherlands\; open to non-EEA-national students enroll
 ed at Dutch art academies.\nAward: EUR 2\,000 each to three commissioned w
 riters\, paid as an advance in September 2026.\nDuration: One-time commiss
 ion\; commissioned texts published at a later date\n\nMore: http://neu-com
 mission.page-not-found.nl/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_mediu
 m=referral
URL:http://neu-commission.page-not-found.nl/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugr
 antdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:The Netherlands\; open to non-EEA-national students enrolled at Du
 tch art academies.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:iwmf-kari-howard-fund-narrative-journalism-2026@artificialnouveau.githu
 b.io
DTSTAMP:20260905T151548Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260712
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260713
SUMMARY:Deadline: IWMF: The Kari Howard Fund for Narrative Journalism 2026
DESCRIPTION:Established in memory of editor Kari Howard\, who championed na
 rrative journalism that wove the music of everyday life into stories illum
 inating the most important issues of the day. Offered by Kari's family and
  friends together with the International Women's Media Foundation\, the fu
 nd supports narrative journalism projects. Grants average around USD 5\,00
 0 (based on previous years). ELIGIBILITY: open to women and nonbinary jour
 nalists. Applicants may be a print journalist or a print journalist leadin
 g a multi-media team\, and may be freelance or staff\; they may apply indi
 vidually or as part of a multi-format team. Professional journalism must b
 e the applicant's primary profession\, with three or more years of profess
 ional experience (internships do not count). Applicants must show proof of
  interest from an editor or a proven track record of publication in promin
 ent media outlets. Applicants must apply and publish in English\; projects
  published anywhere in the world are eligible\, and stories may be publish
 ed digitally (not necessarily in a newspaper or magazine). Any multi-forma
 t reporting must supplement a printed project. All reporting and publishin
 g must be completed within six months of the award. Applicants receive a d
 ecision by early September. DEADLINE: 12 July 2026\, 11:59pm EST.\n\nOrgan
 isation: International Women's Media Foundation (IWMF)\nLocation: Worldwid
 e\; projects reported and published in English anywhere in the world. Open
  to women and nonbinary journalists.\nAward: Grants average around USD 5\,
 000 (based on previous years). No application fee.\nDuration: All reportin
 g and publishing must be completed within six months of the award\n\nMore:
  https://iwmf.submittable.com/submit/c65a15f2-9ff5-4c2b-b2a3-2d897c703381/
 the-kari-howard-fund-for-narrative-journalism-2026?utm_source=artificialno
 uveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://iwmf.submittable.com/submit/c65a15f2-9ff5-4c2b-b2a3-2d897c70338
 1/the-kari-howard-fund-for-narrative-journalism-2026?utm_source=artificial
 nouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Worldwide\; projects reported and published in English anywhere in
  the world. Open to women and nonbinary journalists.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:letterenfonds-project-grants-translators@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260905T151548Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260815
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260816
SUMMARY:Deadline: Nederlands Letterenfonds: Project Grants for Literary Tra
 nslators (August 2026 round)
DESCRIPTION:Project subsidies from the Nederlands Letterenfonds for advance
 d literary translators with a current publishing contract for a translatio
 n from or into Dutch. The next round closes 15 August 2026\; decisions are
  made approximately four months after the deadline (December). ELIGIBILITY
 : literary translators with a substantial published portfolio and a contra
 cted translation project\; primary income must be below EUR 52\,500.\n\nOr
 ganisation: Nederlands Letterenfonds (Dutch Foundation for Literature)\nLo
 cation: Worldwide (literary translators with a contracted translation from
  or into Dutch)\nAward: Project-based subsidy. Income cap EUR 52\,500 for 
 primary income. Standard minimum rates: EUR 0.0802/word for prose\; EUR 2.
 92/line for poetry. No application fee.\nDuration: Project-based\, scaled 
 to the contracted translation\n\nMore: https://www.letterenfonds.nl/en-car
 ibbean/funding/project-grants-for-literary-translators?utm_source=artifici
 alnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.letterenfonds.nl/en-caribbean/funding/project-grants-for-li
 terary-translators?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referr
 al
LOCATION:Worldwide (literary translators with a contracted translation from
  or into Dutch)
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:oif-artist-mobility-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260905T151548Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260831
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260901
SUMMARY:Deadline: OIF: Support for Artist Mobility and Circulation of Cultu
 ral Goods 2026 (Francophonie)
DESCRIPTION:The OIF Support for Artist Mobility and Circulation of Cultural
  Goods programme provides grants of up to EUR 5\,000 for mobility (travel\
 , accommodation\, visa fees\, logistics) and up to EUR 2\,500 for circulat
 ion of cultural goods (excess baggage\, freight\, customs) within the Fran
 cophone zone\; both can be combined. ELIGIBILITY: professional artists and
  established artistic collectives with a demonstrated connection to the Fr
 ancophone space (by nationality\, working language\, or artistic collabora
 tions)\, residing in an OIF member state\, with minimum 2 years of experie
 nce in the cultural or artistic sector\; must directly manage the project 
 (not act as intermediaries)\; one application per individual per call. ELI
 GIBLE DISCIPLINES: live performance (music\, theatre\, dance\, comedy\, st
 orytelling)\, cinema/audiovisual\, literature/publishing\, and visual arts
 . PRIORITY given to projects promoting gender equality\, women artists\, c
 reators under 35\, and South-South mobility. Projects must take place betw
 een 25 March and 30 November 2026. Multiple selection sessions throughout 
 the year\; call open until 31 August 2026. Information webinars: 11 March\
 , 13 May\, and 8 July 2026 at 3 PM Paris time. Contact: culture.dlc@franco
 phonie.org. Apply at https://appelsaprojets.francophonie.org/fr/applicatio
 ns/soutien-a-la-circulation-des-biens-et-mobilite-des-artistes.\n\nOrganis
 ation: Organisation internationale de la Francophonie (OIF)\nLocation: Fra
 ncophone zone (OIF member states globally)\nAward: Up to EUR 5\,000 for ar
 tist mobility (travel\, accommodation\, visas\, logistics). Up to EUR 2\,5
 00 for circulation of cultural goods (excess baggage\, freight\, customs).
  Both can be combined. No application fee.\nDuration: Residencies or tours
  of 5 days to 3 months. Projects must take place between 25 March and 30 N
 ovember 2026.\n\nMore: https://appelsaprojets.francophonie.org/fr/applicat
 ions/soutien-a-la-circulation-des-biens-et-mobilite-des-artistes?utm_sourc
 e=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://appelsaprojets.francophonie.org/fr/applications/soutien-a-la-ci
 rculation-des-biens-et-mobilite-des-artistes?utm_source=artificialnouveaug
 rantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Francophone zone (OIF member states globally)
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:prohelvetia-comic-creation-grant-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260905T151548Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260901
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260902
SUMMARY:Deadline: Comic Creation Grant
DESCRIPTION:Pro Helvetia's comic creation grant supports the development of
  comic projects intended for publication\, including digital formats. Appl
 icants must have published at least one independent work with a profession
 al publisher or the equivalent in magazines. ELIGIBILITY: requires a conne
 ction to Switzerland (Swiss citizenship\, or permanent residency with regu
 lar artistic activity in Switzerland)\; not open to practitioners without 
 a Swiss connection. AMOUNT: maximum CHF 25\,000. Submission deadline 1 Sep
 tember (23:59 CEST). Apply via the Pro Helvetia portal.\n\nOrganisation: P
 ro Helvetia (Swiss Arts Council)\nLocation: Switzerland-based comic creato
 rs.\nAward: Maximum CHF 25\,000. No application fee.\nDuration: Creation p
 hase for a comic project intended for publication\; deadline 1 September.\
 n\nMore: https://prohelvetia.ch/en/find-support/comic-creation-grant?utm_s
 ource=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://prohelvetia.ch/en/find-support/comic-creation-grant?utm_source=
 artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Switzerland-based comic creators.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:prohelvetia-literary-creation-grant-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260905T151548Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260901
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260902
SUMMARY:Deadline: Literary Creation Grant
DESCRIPTION:Pro Helvetia's literary creation grant supports the development
  of literary projects intended for publication\, including fiction\, child
 ren's and youth literature\, poetry\, drama\, and spoken word. Applicants 
 must have prior published work\, a premiere\, or professional performances
 . ELIGIBILITY: requires a connection to Switzerland (Swiss citizenship\, o
 r permanent residency with regular artistic activity in Switzerland)\; not
  open to practitioners without a Swiss connection. AMOUNT: up to CHF 25\,0
 00 for writing\, CHF 18\,000 for theatre texts\, or CHF 15\,000 for perfor
 mative literary projects. Deadlines twice a year: 1 March (23:59 CET) and 
 1 September (23:59 CEST). Apply via the Pro Helvetia portal.\n\nOrganisati
 on: Pro Helvetia (Swiss Arts Council)\nLocation: Switzerland-based authors
  and collectives.\nAward: Up to CHF 25\,000 (writing)\, CHF 18\,000 (theat
 re texts)\, or CHF 15\,000 (performative literary projects). No applicatio
 n fee.\nDuration: Creation phase for a literary project intended for publi
 cation\; deadlines twice yearly (1 March and 1 September).\n\nMore: https:
 //prohelvetia.ch/en/find-support/literary-creation-grant?utm_source=artifi
 cialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://prohelvetia.ch/en/find-support/literary-creation-grant?utm_sour
 ce=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Switzerland-based authors and collectives.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:sloan-foundation-book-grants-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260905T151548Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260901
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260902
SUMMARY:Deadline: Alfred P. Sloan Foundation: Book Grants (Public Understan
 ding of Science and Technology)
DESCRIPTION:The one Sloan program that funds individuals directly: grants f
 or authors researching and writing nonfiction books that bring science and
  technology to a general audience. Over 200 authors supported since 1996. 
 Favoured topics include elucidating confusing or controversial scientific 
 subjects\, profiles of figures in science and technology\, science-technol
 ogy-art connections\, women and science\, and the culture and philosophy o
 f science. Start with a letter of inquiry to program director Doron Weber\
 ; full proposals are by invitation only. Reviewed three times a year: LOIs
  by 1 September (decision by 15 February)\, 1 January (by 31 May) and 1 Ma
 y (by 31 October). No application fee.\n\nOrganisation: Alfred P. Sloan Fo
 undation\nLocation: Remote / anywhere (US foundation\; grants paid directl
 y to authors or via a nonprofit host)\nAward: Typically up to $60\,000 per
  book grant\nDuration: Project-based (book research and writing)\n\nMore: 
 https://sloan.org/programs/public-understanding/books?utm_source=artificia
 lnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://sloan.org/programs/public-understanding/books?utm_source=artifi
 cialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Remote / anywhere (US foundation\; grants paid directly to authors
  or via a nonprofit host)
END:VEVENT
